<title>USA: U.S. Midwest to turn chilly, but winds diminishing.</title>
<headline>U.S. Midwest to turn chilly, but winds diminishing.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sub-freezing weather should move into the U.S. Midwest late Thursday and remain through early Saturday, but the cold should not pose a threat to livestock or crops, meteorologists said.</p>
<p>Forecasts also called for 0.5 to 1.5 inches of rain Thursday along the Red River Valley in Oklahoma and Texas. Snowfall of less than 2.0 inches was forecast for late Thursday and early Friday from the Oklahoma Panhandle to central Kansas.</p>
</text>
